WEBVTT

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:05.620
<v Callum Reid>Morning, everyone. Friday at last. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.259
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, bit tinny, but you're there.</v>

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.419
<v David Whitfield>Unfortunately, yes.</v>

00:00:12.859 --> 00:00:19.160
<v Callum Reid>Lovely. Whose new car's that in the car park, then? Taking up about a space and a half.</v>

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:24.210
<v Jamie Brennan>Not mine. Mine's the one worth less than the tyres on that.</v>

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.160
<v Hannah Price>It's parked diagonally for extra prestige.</v>

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:35.100
<v Priya Raman>Never mind the car, the heating in the portakabin's absolutely roasting. I've got the window open in April.</v>

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:39.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>You've found the only warm bit of the factory.</v>

00:00:39.609 --> 00:00:43.109
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, apparently all the heat's been allocated to my chair.</v>

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:51.869
<v Callum Reid>Right, before we get into heating policy. Marcus Hale and Sarah Okafor aren't with us today. Dave, how are you getting on?</v>

00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:00.170
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, so the risk assessment for work on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve, I've updated that. All done.</v>

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:03.229
<v Callum Reid>Good, cheers.</v>

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:08.859
<v David Whitfield>And CV01, jam's cleared and I've checked the sensors. All fine, that's sorted.</v>

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.349
<v Priya Raman>Ah, good.</v>

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:20.189
<v David Whitfield>Only other thing from me, I heard a slight rattle from the Main Water Isolation Valve. Nothing to action yet, just an observation.</v>

00:01:21.569 --> 00:01:22.769
<v Callum Reid>Okay, understood. Hannah?</v>

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:30.379
<v Hannah Price>The pressure-drop investigation, I'm still on it. Got a bit further with it, going fine so far.</v>

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.579
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. Olu, you had an update as well?</v>

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:41.099
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah, the replacement parts from Northfield. Went over, picked them up, all done. No issues found.</v>

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.430
<v Jamie Brennan>Nice. An uneventful parts run, for once.</v>

00:01:46.769 --> 00:01:52.370
<v Callum Reid>And I've made a start on organising the toolbox talk for the team. That's ticking along.</v>

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.540
<v Priya Raman>Okay, cheers.</v>

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:06.230
<v Callum Reid>One from the boss, in her absence: the sensor recalibration on the heater box on one is moving over to Hannah Price. Hannah, you okay taking that over?</v>

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.409
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll take over that recalibration.</v>

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:11.580
<v Callum Reid>Thanks. Right, today's new bits.</v>

00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:20.729
<v Callum Reid>First, stores Jamie, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the pick and place on two? That one's safety critical, straight away.</v>

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.680
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah. You mean sorting both the permit and the isolation, not just the paperwork?</v>

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.659
<v Callum Reid>Both, yeah. That's the immediate one.</v>

00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:38.729
<v Jamie Brennan>Understood, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the pick and place on two straight away.</v>

00:02:41.030 --> 00:02:43.479
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, sensible. No ambiguity on that one.</v>

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:46.909
<v Callum Reid>Exactly.</v>

00:02:48.409 --> 00:02:52.259
<v Jamie Brennan>Okay, I'm with you. What else have you got for me?</v>

00:02:54.030 --> 00:03:04.180
<v Callum Reid>Jamie, can you go to Kestrel in Leeds to pick up the replacement parts for the feed pump after lunch? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:12.979
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll go to Kestrel in Leeds after lunch and pick up the replacement parts for the feed pump.</v>

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.979
<v David Whitfield>Yeah, that's the production hold-up at the minute.</v>

00:03:19.659 --> 00:03:21.759
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, first as in before the—</v>

00:03:24.219 --> 00:03:31.919
<v Callum Reid>No, sorry, talking over you. Safety one straight away. After lunch, the parts run needs doing first because production's waiting on it.</v>

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:36.280
<v Jamie Brennan>Got you. Immediate safety bit, then the collection first after lunch.</v>

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:41.199
<v Hannah Price>Friday in Leeds. Living the dream, Jamie.</v>

00:03:42.289 --> 00:03:45.439
<v Jamie Brennan>Oh, absolutely. All the glamour ends up in stores.</v>

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:55.629
<v Callum Reid>Last one, stores Jamie: can you do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the little water valve on two for Monday? Top priority please.</v>

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:04.509
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the little water valve on two for Monday. Top priority, understood.</v>

00:04:05.669 --> 00:04:08.120
<v Priya Raman>Sorry, was that Monday? Your audio clipped.</v>

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:10.479
<v Callum Reid>Monday, yes.</v>

00:04:12.969 --> 00:04:15.069
<v Jamie Brennan>That's clear. Three for me, then.</v>

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:17.750
<v Callum Reid>Yep, those three.</v>

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.220
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Audio's gone a bit underwater again.</v>

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:27.279
<v David Whitfield>Might just be how we sound by Friday.</v>

00:04:29.579 --> 00:04:32.730
<v Priya Raman>No, definitely Teams. Though I wouldn't rule it out.</v>

00:04:34.379 --> 00:04:38.230
<v Callum Reid>Right, we'll leave it there before I turn into a submarine.</v>

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:39.769
<v Hannah Price>Cheers, everyone.</v>

00:04:40.069 --> 00:04:41.269
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers.</v>

00:04:43.329 --> 00:04:44.529
<v Callum Reid>Thanks all. Bye.</v>
